We observe that, up to moderate friction coefficients ($\mu_p \leq 0.4$), Figure \ref{fig:dissipation_normal_tangential}a, the power dissipated due to collisions decreases as particles become more elongated or flattened for aspect ratios $M_\alpha>1.2$.

Owing to the system's structural anisotropy, assuming all particles are perfectly aligned with their major axis along the flow direction, the cross-sectional areas of each grain are listed in Table \ref{tab:cross_sections} 
