\section{Spatial distribution of contacts}
\label{app:global_contact_distribution}

We bin forces in the global reference frame $(x,y,z)$ by the angle they make with $x$ axis in the $xy$ plane.
We compute the probability of having a force at a certain angular location, $\rho$, which satisfies the following normalization condition:
\begin{align}
    \int_0^{2 \pi} \rho(\beta) d\beta = 1 \, ,
\end{align}
and the average force, conditional to a force being present $\overline{F}$, projected in the $xy$ plane.
