\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.55\linewidth]{Figures/fig_rule_16485732.pdf}
  \label{fig:class_1a_dynamics}
  \label{Ia_rule}
\end{figure}

The model is $\mathcal{C}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{T}$ symmetric, but it does not possess independent $\mathcal{C}$, $\mathcal{P}$ or $\mathcal{T}$ symmetries. Due to the absence of $\mathcal{P}$ symmetry, its correlation functions are not symmetric under $x\rightarrow -x$. We present the correlation functions of range-1 local observables (see Section~\ref{sec:CF}) in Figure~\ref{fig:class_1_correlator}. Both correlators decay exponentially with similar rates.
