\section{General Linear Programs for UCE}
\label{app:general-uce-lp}

We now provide the UCE primal and dual LPs for the most general case where prices may be fully nonlinear and non-anonymous, used to develop iterative combinatorial auctions for general valuations~\citep{parkes1999bundle,ausubel2002ascending,mishra2007ascending}. We first begin with the primal and dual LP formulations for CE prices. These LPs correspond to the \emph{third order assignment} formulation for a single seller provided in~\cite{bikhchandani2002package}.

To accommodate this more general formulation we vary the notation somewhat from the main body of the paper. Let $\mX$ be the space of bundles, and let $\Gamma$ be the set of feasible allocations. We use $x \in \mX$ to denote a bundle and $\vy = (y_1, \dots, y_n)$ to denote an allocation where each $i \in N$ obtains bundle $y_i$.
%
The allocation LP (primal) is as follows. There is a variable $z_i(x) \in [0,1]$ to indicate that agent $i$ obtains bundle $x$, for all $x \in \mX$, and a variable $\vy \in [0,1]$ to indicate that allocation $\vy \in \Gamma$ is selected on the seller's side.
%
\begin{alignat}{3}
   \max_{z \geq 0, \delta \geq 0} & \qquad \ds \sum_{i \in N} \sum_{x \in \mX} v_i(x) z_i(x) && \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[\mu]$} & \qquad \ds \sum_{\vy \in \Gamma} \delta(\vy) \leq 1 && \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[\pi_i]$} & \qquad \ds \sum_{x \in \mX} z_i(x) \leq 1 && \qquad \mbox{$\forall i \in N$} \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[p_i(x)]$} & \qquad \ds z_i(x) \leq \sum_{\vy \in \Gamma : x = y_i} \delta(\vy) && \qquad \mbox{$\forall i \in N$, $\forall x \in \mX$} \nonumber
\end{alignat}
%
(The dual variables for each constraint type are given on the left.) The dual is as follows. There is a variable $\pi_i \geq 0$ for each $i \in N$ which corresponds to agent's $i$ utility, a variable $\mu \geq 0$ corresponding to the seller's revenue, and variables $p_i(x)$ for each $i \in N$, $x \in \mX$ representing personalized bundle prices.
%
\begin{alignat}{3}
\min_{\pi \geq 0, \mu \geq 0, p \geq 0} & \qquad \ds \sum_{i \in N} \pi_i + \mu && \nonumber \\
\mbox{$[z_i(x)]$} & \qquad \ds \pi_i \geq v_i(x) - p_i(x) && \qquad \mbox{$\forall i \in S$, $\forall x \in \mX$} \nonumber \\
\mbox{$[\delta(\vy)]$} & \qquad \ds \mu \geq \sum_{i \in S} p(y_i) && \qquad \mbox{$\forall \vy \in \Gamma$} \nonumber
\end{alignat}
%

To form the LP for a UCE, we follow the recipe provided in Section~\ref{sec:primal-dual-auction}. We make copies of the variable, and constraints for the main and marginal economies, and the objective function is the sum of the objectives across variables copies. Next, we split the buyer utility constraints into two by replacing the price term with a lower envelope price term. Note that we only split the buyer utility constraints, not the seller revenue constraints.
%
\begin{alignat}{3}
\min_{\pi \geq 0, \mu \geq 0, p \geq 0, \alpha \geq 0,  \rho\: \mathrm{free}} & \qquad \ds \sum_{j \in N_0} \left[ \sum_{i \in \Nj} \pi_i^{-j} + \mu^{-j} \right] && \nonumber \\
\mbox{$[z_i^{-j}(x)]$} & \qquad \ds \pi_i^{-j} \geq v_i(x) - \rho_i(x) && \qquad \mbox{$\forall j \in N_0$, $\forall i \in \Nj$, $\forall x \in \mX$} \nonumber \\
\mbox{$[\beta_i^{-j}(x)]$} & \qquad \ds \rho_i(x) \leq p_i^{-j}(x) + \alpha_i^{-j} && \qquad \mbox{$\forall j \in N_0$, $\forall i \in \Nj$, $\forall x \in \mX$} \nonumber \\
\mbox{$[\delta^{-j}(\vy)]$} & \qquad \ds \mu^{-j} \geq \sum_{i \in \Nj} p_i^{-j}(y_i) + \alpha_i^{-j} && \qquad \mbox{$\forall j \in N_0$, $\forall \vy \in \Gamma$} \nonumber
\end{alignat}
%
The dual of this LP, which we have referred to as the Primal UCE LP, is as follows. By restricting it to demanded bundles, it forms the basis of the primal-dual algorithm.
%
\begin{alignat}{3}
   \max_{z \geq 0, \delta \geq 0, \beta \geq 0} & \qquad \ds \sum_{j \in N_0} \left[ \sum_{i \in \Nj} \sum_{x \in \mX} v_i(x) z_i^{-j}(x) \right] && \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[\mu^{-j}]$} & \qquad \ds \sum_{\vy \in \Gamma} \delta^{-j}(\vy) \leq 1 && \qquad \mbox{$\forall j \in N_0$} \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[\pi_i^{-j}]$} & \qquad \ds \sum_{x \in \mX} z_i^{-j}(x) \leq 1 && \qquad \mbox{$\forall j \in N_0$, $\forall i \in \Nj$} \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[\rho_i(x)]$} & \qquad \ds \sum_{j \in N_0^{-i}} z_i^{-j}(x) = \sum_{j \in N_0^{-i}} \beta_i^{-j}(x) && \qquad \mbox{$\forall i \in N$, $\forall x \in \mX$} \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[\alpha_i^{-j}]$} & \qquad \ds \sum_{x \in \mX} \beta_i^{-j}(x) \leq \sum_{\vy \in \Gamma} \delta^{-j}(\vy) && \qquad \mbox{$\forall j \in N_0$, $\forall i \in \Nj$} \nonumber \\
   \mbox{$[p_i^{-j}(x)]$} & \qquad \ds \beta_i^{-j}(x) \leq \sum_{\vy \in \Gamma : x = y_i} \delta^{-j}(\vy) && \qquad \mbox{$\forall j \in N_0$, $\forall i \in N^{-j}$ $\forall x \in \mX$} \nonumber
\end{alignat}

