\caption{\small Structure of Maxiumum Caliber model parameters, interpretable as rates of ecological processes. (A) The $\eta_{ij}$'s represent the interactions between (blue) and within (green) species in the same patch, as well as rates of colonization among patches (red). The $\lambda_i$'s correspond to the rate of background colonization of a species to a patch. (B) Four different community structures (motifs) used to test Maximum Caliber modeling. Each example system consists of three species found in three possible patches. The heatmaps show example $\eta_{ij}$ values (red for positive and blue for negative) for each motif.}
