\section{Discussion}
We pretrained 4 different TFMs with \bmfmrna{} indicating the comprehensiveness of our software. 
The different pretraining decisions are exposed to the user via the YAML interface, and required no changes to the code.
We reported detailed metrics on cell type annotation on cell type clustering tasks. Our results show that pretraining with a small number of selectively sampled cells can match or even exceed the performance of models pretrained with 10 or 100 times more cells. 
As shown in Table 3, WCED 1pct + Multitask achieved similar performance when compared with \scGPT{} model on overall zero-shot embedding quality. 
Further, WCED 10\% on an average achieved 3.7 percentage points better performance than \scGPT, indicating the generalization of WCED method for cell type annotation tasks. 
As shown in Table 6, finetuned WCED 10\% performed comparable or better than \scGPT{} further indicating the strength of WCED approach. 
Figure \ref{fig:umap-cellxgene-heldout} shows that the embeddings and the predictions from the multitask learning are robust, even when applied to new datasets.
At the same time, as we show in Fig. \ref{fig:umap-wced-multi-pbmc-10k}, the zero shot embeddings capture subtle biological patterns such as the gradual cell-type differentiation from stem cells, to progenitors to fully differentiated cells, on unseen data.

