\section{Conclusions and Future work}
We developed \bmfmrna , a transcriptomic foundation model software package that includes configurable pretraining strategies adapted from existing  TFMs. 
We also added a novel methodology, WCED, that is suitable for non-sequential nature of transcriptomic data, an evaluation benchmark suite for multiple single-cell machine learning tasks, and utilities to gain deeper understanding of the model insights. We demonstrate that \bmfmrna  allows to build multiple variations of TFMs through hydra configurations. 
We also show that models built using \bmfmrna  package on a small subset of \cellxgene{} dataset achieves similar results on cell-type clustering and annotation tasks when compared to existing models. In future, we plan to report detailed results on other benchmark tasks such as perturbation prediction and gene regulatory network inference. 
By open-sourcing our package at \url{https://github.com/BiomedSciAI/biomed-multi-omic} and inviting community contributions, we enable the collaborative development of TFMs to deepen biological understanding and accelerate target and drug discovery in the future.




