Thus there exists $m$ and $z\in p^{1/p^m}((x,y)R^+)^{epf}$ such that $z\notin (x,y)R^+_Q$. We may assume that $x,y,z\in S$ where $S$ is a complete normal local domain module-finite over $R$. Let $P$ be the contraction of $Q$ to $S$ and let $T$ be the $(PS_P)$-adic completion of $S_P$. Since $S_P$ is excellent and normal, $T$ is a Noetherian complete 
