 \end{eqnarray}}
 When the manufacturers quote prices $(p_i, p_j)$ with $p_i = p_j$, the fraction of NLDP customers get divided equally among  the two manufacturers. Hence from \eqref{demand_function} and \eqref{eqn_util_manu}, their utility functions (with $p_i=p_j$) are given by:
