Then $\xi_i \times \xi_j$ is the equilibrium cycle for the lower level game between the two manufacturers. 
\end{thm}
{\textbf{Remarks} The above mentioned equilibrium cycle doesn't  consist the action $n_o$ for both the manufacturers, which implies that the cycle doesn't stop when one manufacturer breakeven point which is a key difference from Edgeworth Cycle (\cite{Maskin}).}



\subsection{ Solution of $\G(q)$ after partial choking point  }
It is important to observe that after $q$ reaches $\bqd$, one manufacturer chooses action $n_o$ and thus the other manufacturer gets utility $W_4(\cdot)$ in \eqref{eqn_W_4}. The operating manufacturer will get the following best utility (see \cite[Lemma 4]{Wadhwa}) :
\begin{eqnarray}\label{eq_W_4_star}
   W_4^{*} = \left \{ \begin{array}{ll}
   \frac{\left(\dbar(1+\varepsilon) - \alpha(1-\varepsilon)(C_\sM + q)\right)^2}{4\alpha(1-\varepsilon)} - O_\sM  &  \mbox{ if } q \le \bqm  \\
   0   & \mbox{ else.}
   \end{array} \right  .  
\end{eqnarray}
where $\bqm = \nicefrac{\dbar(1+\varepsilon) - \alpha C_\sM(1-\varepsilon)- 2\sqrt{\alpha O_\sM}}{\alpha(1-\varepsilon)}$. 
Now if the supplier further increases the value of q to \( \bqm \) both the manufacturers will stop operating and will exit the market. In view of this we refer this point as \textit{complete choking point} as no manufacturers will sustain in the market after supplier quotes a price larger than $\bqm$.







Now define the following:
\begin{eqnarray}\label{eqn_pmu}
    \pmu = \arg\max_{p_i}W_4(p_i)
\end{eqnarray}
and $\pml$ is a {\color{red}unique} point which satifes the following:
\begin{eqnarray}\label{eqn_pml}
W_1(\pml,\pml) = 0    
\end{eqnarray}
which can be interpreted as follows:
\begin{eqnarray*}
\lim_{p_i\uparrow\pml}U_i(p_i,\pml;q) = 0
\end{eqnarray*}



\begin{thm}\label{thm_eq_cy_aft_qbar}
  For any $ \bqm \ge q >    \bqd$ and for symmetric manufacturers.
Define

\begin{eqnarray}
    \xi_i \times \ \xi_j = n_o \cup
    \left[ \pml, \pmu \right ]^2
\end{eqnarray}

Then $\xi_i \times \xi_j$ is the equilibrium cycle for the lower level game between the two manufacturers.   
\end{thm}





