\subsection{Effect of the infection rate $(\gamma)$ on the TB-infected population} 
In Figure \ref{fig:gamma_infected}, we demonstrate the impact of the infection rate $\gamma$ on the number of infected individuals. The numerical results were obtained by varying the value of the infectious rate $\gamma$ while keeping the other parameters constant. In the deterministic model, when the value of the infection rate increased from 0.075 to 0.227, there was also an increase in the number of infected individuals as in the exposed cases. 
%
