\begin{abstract}
For a subfield $\KK$ of $\CC$, we denote by $\C^{\KK}$ the category of algebras of functions defined on the globally subanalytic sets that are generated by all $\KK$-powers and logarithms of positively-valued globally subanalytic functions.  For any function $f\in\C^\KK(\RR)$, we study links between holomorphic extensions of $f$ and the decay of its Fourier transform $\hbox{\calliBig F}[f]$ by using tameness properties of the globally subanalytic functions from which $f$ is constructed.  We first prove a number of theorems about analytic continuation of functions in $\C^{\KK}$, including the fact that $f\in\C^{\KK}(\RR)$ extends meromorphically to $\CC$ if and only if $f$ is rational.  We then characterize the exponential rate of decay of $\hbox{\calliBig F}[f]$ by the maximal width of a horizontal strip in the plane about the real axis to which $f$ extends holomorphically.  Finally, we show that $\hbox{\calliBig F}[f]$ is integrable if $f$ is integrable and continuous.
\end{abstract}

