It has been recently shown that the corner term to the entanglement entropy exists, has a universal logarithmic form, and can serve as an entanglement susceptibility for all three of these universality classes \cite{Yu2008, Kovacs2012-rtfim, Kovacs2012-percolation, Kovacs2024-qmcp}, at least for square subsystems, as shown in figure~\ref{fig:grp}. %, it has been recently shown that quantum entanglement has a universal logarithmic correction due to the corners of the subsystem at all three IDFPs.
%this correction has been found to be logarithmic with a universal prefactor \cite{Kovacs2012-rtfim, Kovacs2012-percolation, Kovacs2024-qmcp}. 
Although being universal, the corner term must depend on the shape (i.e., opening angle) of the subsystem corners \cite{WK-corner-entanglement}, however this has not been explored for the generic QCP and the QMCP. 

