\subsubsection{The effectiveness of Bit-Decoding.}
We compare the SpMM performance in Libra (TCU-only pattern) with different data access patterns, including those based on TCF~\cite{wang2023tc} and ME-TCF~\cite{dtc} formats, as well as our Bit-Decoding. As shown in Table~\ref{tab:ab_format}, in the case of SpMM, Bit-Decoding outperforms the ME-TCF across all 500 matrices, with 76.2\% of the matrices achieving a speedup greater than $1.2\times$, with an average speedup of $1.3\times$.
Furthermore, in the case of SDDMM, the performance advantage of Bit-Decoding is even more pronounced, achieving an average speedup of $2.6\times$ compared to ME-TCF. This improvement mainly stems from each thread directly identifying its write-back position based on its thread ID, eliminating the need to traverse all preceding non-zero elements in the TC block during SDDMM operator.


